      "id": "claim_be2d4a8c8160404385e6da6a1f9b999a",
      "statement": "docsweep/server/security.py's module docstring establishes the security posture: the server binds to 127.0.0.1 only, a token is required, and any path the server lets a client view/preview/open must resolve under a configured scan root after realpath resolution.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docsweep/server/security.py#L1-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a6f7650b932c5d79db8116035c139ddbbd89e4423a646261de8e936a07d790e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_994a718f2b5244c6842eb3f3984f3b5e",
      "statement": "check_token() accepts a token from an HttpOnly cookie, an X-Docsweep-Token header, or a query parameter, comparing each with secrets.compare_digest, and app.py's _token_cookie_exchange middleware exchanges a valid first-visit ?token= query parameter for a SameSite=Strict HttpOnly cookie via a 302 redirect for GET/HEAD, but answers POST requests in place instead of redirecting because redirecting a POST would downgrade many clients to GET.",
      "evidence": [
