    {
      "id": "claim_30285e8bcc474e568fa51119e5f1c1b8",
      "statement": "Every server response carries a Content-Security-Policy of script-src 'self' with no 'unsafe-inline' (plus Referrer-Policy: no-referrer and X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff), set by an _security_headers middleware, so that a hypothetical script payload that evaded sanitization still cannot execute in the browser; style-src does allow 'unsafe-inline' as a narrower, lower-risk exception for the board's inline health-bar width styling.",
      "evidence": [
